# Chess.com integration — decisions

## API boundary
**Chose:** Call Chess.com’s public player, stats, archive, and monthly-game endpoints through TanStack server functions.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — `src/lib/chesscom.functions.ts` establishes the server boundary, but no rationale was found for it over direct browser calls.

## HTTP behavior
**Chose:** Send a configurable product User-Agent and retry failed or rate-limited requests with backoff.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — `src/lib/chesscom.ts` and `.env.example` define this behavior, but no in-repo policy rationale was found.

## Game identity
**Chose:** Normalize Chess.com game URLs to the pathname and use `(username, game_link)` as the game upsert key.
**Considered:** Keeping the full URL.
**Why:** The normalization comment says: “Keep path only — live/daily ids are unique enough” (source: `src/lib/chesscom.ts`).

## PGN header parsing
**Chose:** Parse headers with lightweight regular expressions inside the Chess.com client instead of importing chess.js at module top level.
**Considered:** Top-level chess.js parsing.
**Why:** The code says this avoids pulling chess.js into the module’s SSR bundle (source: `gameFromPgn` in `src/lib/chesscom.ts`).

## Supported games
**Chose:** Import standard chess games with PGN and skip variants.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — the filter and UI message are explicit, but no rationale for excluding variants was found.

## Played date
**Chose:** Prefer Chess.com `endTime` over PGN date headers.
**Considered:** `[Date]` and `[UTCDate]`.
**Why:** `src/lib/analysis/analyzeGame.ts` notes that daily games keep their start date in those PGN headers.

## Primary rating
**Chose:** Prefer blitz, then rapid, bullet, and daily when selecting a rating for puzzle matching.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — the order is documented in `src/lib/chesscom.ts`, but its rationale was not found.
